data: {"text":"1. That the Complainant, Mr. Manoj Kumar Tirkey, S/o Shri Laxman Tirkey, aged 35 years, R/o Quarter No. B-12, HEC Township,"}

data: {"text":" Dhurwa, Ranchi - 834004, is a 'consumer' within the meaning of Section 2(7) of the Consumer Protection Act, 2019, having purchased goods for"}

data: {"text":" consideration which is paid or promised or partly"}

data: {"text":" paid and partly promised, or under any system of deferred payment and includes"}

data: {"text":" any beneficiary of such goods other than the person who makes such payment.\n\n2. That the"}

data: {"text":" Opposite Party, Reliance Digital Retail Ltd., Ground Floor, Nucleus Mall, East Jail Road, Ranchi - 834001, is a company engaged in the business of retail sale of consumer dur"}

data: {"text":"ables including refrigerators and other home appliances, and provides after-sales service through its authorized service network"}

data: {"text":".\n\n3. That on 25.02.2026, the Complainant purchased a Whirlpool 300L Double Door Refrigerator (Model IF INV CNV 355 COOL ILLUSIA) from the Opposite Party's store at Nucleus Mall,"}

data: {"text":" Ranchi for a consideration of Rs. 42,990/- vide Invoice No. RD-RAN-2026-008741. The said amount was paid via Debit card transaction through"}

data: {"text":" SBI card ending with 7890.\n\n4. That the refrigerator was delivered to the Complainant's residence"}

data: {"text":" on 27.02.2026 and was installed by the Opposite Party's technician on the same day. The installation was completed and"}

data: {"text":" the unit was tested for functionality before the technician left the premises.\n\n5. That within 15 days of installation, on 14.03.2026, the"}

data: {"text":" compressor of the refrigerator started making loud rattling noises and the cooling capacity dropped significantly, rendering the appliance def"}

data: {"text":"ective and unfit for its intended purpose. The Complainant immediately informed the Opposite Party's service centre and raised service"}

data: {"text":" ticket No. WP-RAN-22891 on 15.03.2026.\n\n6. That despite raising the complaint prompt"}

data: {"text":"ly, two technicians visited the Complainant's residence on 20.03.2026 and 10.04.2026 respectively, but could not resolve the issue. The Opposite Party has refused to replace the def"}

data: {"text":"ective unit, claiming the sounds to be 'normal operational sounds' despite the product clearly being defective and"}

data: {"text":" not functioning as per specifications. The Complainant's emails"}

data: {"text":" dated 25.03.2026 and 20.04.2026 seeking replacement of the defective unit have been ignored by the Opposite Party.\n\n7. That the conduct"}

data: {"text":" of the Opposite Party amounts to 'deficiency in service' within the meaning of Section 2(11) of the Consumer Protection Act, 2019, and the supplied refrigerator constitutes a"}

data: {"text":" 'defect' within the meaning of Section 2(10) of the said Act. The refusal to replace a clearly def"}

data: {"text":"ective product and ignoring the consumer's legitimate grievances constitutes an 'unfair trade practice' within the meaning of Section 2"}

data: {"text":"(47) of the Consumer Protection Act, 2019.\n\n8. That this Hon'ble Commission has territorial jurisdiction to"}

data: {"text":" entertain the present complaint as the cause of action arose at Ranchi where the goods were purchased, delivered, and where the deficiency in service manifested. The Opposite Party"}

data: {"text":"'s store and authorized service centre are also located at Ranchi, being within the territorial jurisdiction of this Hon'ble Commission.\n\n9. That this"}

data: {"text":" Hon'ble Commission has pecuniary jurisdiction to entertain the present complaint as the total claim including refund and compensation amounts to Rs. 82,990/-, which falls well"}

data: {"text":" within the pecuniary jurisdiction of the District Commission (up to Rs. 50 Lakh as per the Consumer Protection Act (Jurisdiction) Notification dated 21 December 2021)."}

data: {"text":"\n\n10. That the present complaint is filed well within the limitation period prescribed under Section 69 of the Consumer Protection Act, 2019. The cause of action arose on 14.03"}

data: {"text":".2026 when the defect manifested and continues till date due to the Opposite Party's persistent refusal to provide"}

data: {"text":" remedy. The complaint is being filed within two years from the date when the cause of action arose.\n\n11. That due"}

data: {"text":" to the defective product and deficiency in service by the Opposite Party, the Complainant has"}

data: {"text":" suffered mental agony, harassment, and inconvenience. The Complainant has been deprived of the use of a functional refrigerator despite paying"}

data: {"text":" the full consideration, and has been forced to approach this Hon'ble Commission for redressal, thereby"}

data: {"text":" incurring litigation costs.\n\n12. That the Complainant is entitled to refund of the purchase amount of Rs. 42,990/-,"}

data: {"text":" compensation for mental agony and harassment in the sum of Rs. 30,000/-, and litigation costs of Rs. 10,000/- along with interest"}

data: {"text":" at the rate of 9% per annum from the date of purchase till realization."}

